    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d86">

                <pb facs="0106" n="92" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg92"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">500.CC/77</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2644</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-06-03">June 3,
                        1944</date>.<lb/>[Received June 19.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my telegram no. 961 of
                    June 2, 2 p.m.,<anchor n="88" xml:id="d86-f1"/> in regard to the participation
                    of China in the Washington conference<anchor n="89" xml:id="d86-f2"/> for the
                    discussion of plans for post-war organization for world security, I have the
                    honor to enclose copy of a memorandum of my conversation on the morning of June
                    2d, with Dr. T. V. Soong, the Minister for Foreign Affairs, when he expressed
                    Chinese appreciation of the American position that China as an Asiatic power
                    should be represented at the conference and requested me to transmit to the
                    President a message from Generalissimo Chiang Kai-shek on the subject.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>C. E. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>



                <xi:include href="d86-a1.xml" xpointer="d86-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d86-a2.xml" xpointer="d86-a2"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d86-f1" n="88" xml:id="d86-f1-content">
